== Part A: game K ==
u1 = -9*p*q/4 + p + 2*q + 1 ; u2 = -9*p*q/4 + 2*p + q + 1
pure payoffs of player 1: (A,A) 7/4 (A,Y) 2 (Y,A) 3 (Y,Y) 1
[Sec 3, Sec 4 example] mixed security level v = 17/9 attained by p = 8/9
pure security level = 7/4
(u1 + u2)/2 - 2 = -(-6*e + 3*s - 4)*(6*e + 3*s - 4)/16 ; (u1 - u2)/2 = -e
[Prop K proof] identity (u1+u2)/2 - 2 = -(3s/4 - 1)^2 + 9e^2/4: True ; so min(u1,u2) - 2 = -(3s/4 - 1)^2 + 9e^2/4 - |e|
[Prop K proof] value at s = 2 - 2|e| for 4/9 < |e| <= 1/2: E/2 - 1/4
[Prop K, Sec 4 example] exact grid 1/180: max of min(u1,u2) = 2 at [('0', '1'), ('2/3', '2/3'), ('1', '0')]
[Prop K] sigma0 = (2/3,2/3) pays (Fraction(2, 1), Fraction(2, 1)) ; (A,Y) pays (Fraction(2, 1), Fraction(3, 1)) ; (Y,A) pays (Fraction(3, 1), Fraction(2, 1))
[Sec 4 example] common path c(t) = 3 - (3 - v) e^{-t} = 17/9 ... reaches (2,2) at t = [log(10/9)]
[Sec 5 leximin] K, grid 1/180: max smallest gain = 1/9 at [('0', '1'), ('2/3', '2/3'), ('1', '0')] ; leximin = [('0', '1'), ('1', '0')]
[Sec 5 leximin] K with player 2's payoffs doubled, grid 1/180: max smallest gain = 2/9 at [('0', '1')] (argument: smallest gain >= 2/9 needs u1 >= 19/9 > 2 and u2 >= 2, so min(u1,u2) = 2 with u1 > 2: only (Y,A))
[Sec 5 discrete step] K: M(v,v) = (3,3), t* = (2 - v)/(3 - v) = 1/10 -> (2,2), then t* = 0

== Part B: prisoner's dilemmas ==
PD (10, 3, 1, 0) : u1 = -6*p*q - p + 9*q + 1 ; v = 1 ; f(p) = -6*p**2 + 8*p + 1 ; p* = 2/3 ; f* = 11/3 ; T+S <= 2R: False
  grid 1/120: max of min(u1,u2) = 11/3 at [('2/3', '2/3')]
  [Prop S] u2 >= P iff q <= 9*p/(6*p + 1) ; q = 1 feasible iff p >= [1/3] (theta = 1/3 ); on q = 1: u1 = 10 - 7*p ; on the binding curve u1 = g(p), g'(p) = -40*(3*p - 1)*(3*p + 2)/(6*p + 1)**2
  [Prop S] max of u1 over IR = 23/3 at (theta, 1) = (1/3, 1) ; f* = 11/3 ; serial outcome pays ( 23/3 , 1 )
  [Sec 5 discrete step] t* = (f* - v)/(M1 - v) = 2/5
PD (5, 3, 1, 0) : u1 = -p*q - p + 4*q + 1 ; v = 1 ; f(p) = -p**2 + 3*p + 1 ; p* = 1 ; f* = 3 ; T+S <= 2R: True
  grid 1/120: max of min(u1,u2) = 3 at [('1', '1')]
  [Prop S] u2 >= P iff q <= 4*p/(p + 1) ; q = 1 feasible iff p >= [1/3] (theta = 1/3 ); on q = 1: u1 = 5 - 2*p ; on the binding curve u1 = g(p), g'(p) = -5*(p - 1)*(p + 3)/(p + 1)**2
  [Prop S] max of u1 over IR = 13/3 at (theta, 1) = (1/3, 1) ; f* = 3 ; serial outcome pays ( 13/3 , 1 )
  [Sec 5 discrete step] t* = (f* - v)/(M1 - v) = 3/5

== Part C: chicken ==
chicken (0, 3, 1, 2) : u1 = -2*p*q + p - q + 2 ; v = 1 ; u1 + u2 = -4*(p*q - 1) ; f(p) = -2*(p - 1)*(p + 1) ; f* = 2 at p = 0 ; u1 + u2 - 2f* = -4*p*q
  [Sec 5 discrete step] M(v,v) = ( 3 , 3 ) since (A,Y) pays (3, 1) ; t* = (f* - v)/(M - v) = 1/2
Aumann's chicken (0, 7, 2, 6) : u1 = -3*p*q + p - 4*q + 6 ; v = 2 ; u1 + u2 = -3*(2*p*q + p + q - 4) ; f(p) = -3*(p - 1)*(p + 2) ; f* = 6 at p = 0 ; u1 + u2 - 2f* = -3*(2*p*q + p + q)
  [Sec 5 discrete step] M(v,v) = ( 7 , 7 ) since (A,Y) pays (7, 2) ; t* = (f* - v)/(M - v) = 4/5

== Part D: game G2 ==
u1 = 7*p*q - 2*p - 3*q + 1 ; v1 = 1/7 at p = 3/7 ; v2 = -1/7 at q = 2/7
u1 - v1 = (7*p - 3)*(7*q - 2)/7
[Remark movers] player 3 on q = 2/7: 19/7 - 2*p range (5/7, 19/7) ; on p = 3/7: 15/7 - q range (8/7, 15/7)

== Part E: traveler's dilemma ==
M = 3 r = 3/2 : u1 + u2 <= 2M with equality only at (M,M): True
M = 10 r = 2 : u1 + u2 <= 2M with equality only at (M,M): True
M = 100 r = 2 : u1 + u2 <= 2M with equality only at (M,M): True
M = 100 r = 1/2 : u1 + u2 <= 2M with equality only at (M,M): True

== Part F: game G3 (players 1 and 2 move, player 3 has one strategy) ==
u1 = 6*p*q - 2*p - 3*q + 3 ; v1 = v2 = 2 at p = 1/2 ; v3 = min(0,1,2,3) = 0
[Remark movers] gains at (a,b) = (2, 2, 0) ; at (a',b') = (1, 1, 3) ; sorted: [0, 2, 2] vs [1, 1, 3]

== Part G: Raiffa's midpoint step in K ==
[Sec 5 bargaining] from (v,v) = (17/9,17/9) the midpoint of the ideal points is ( 22/9 , 22/9 ), above the largest common payoff 2, so outside H
done
